## PHASE 4: INTEGRATION VALIDATION

### Task 4.1 — End-to-End Flows
| ID | Flow | Steps to Validate |
|----|------|-------------------|
| 4.1.1 | **Signup → Subscribe → Use → Cancel** | Auth → Checkout → Stripe webhook → Plan upgrade → Use features → Cancel → Downgrade |
| 4.1.2 | **API Key lifecycle** | Create key → Authenticate → Make API calls → Rate limit hit → Revoke key |
| 4.1.3 | **Webhook lifecycle** | Register webhook → Trigger event → Delivery queued → Executed → Retry on fail → Abandon |
| 4.1.4 | **Admin Plan Management** | Create plan → Set limits → User subscribes → Limits enforced → Edit plan → Limits update |
| 4.1.5 | **Feature Flag Flow** | Admin creates flag → Flag cached in Redis → SaaS checks flag → Toggle off → Feature hidden |
| 4.1.6 | **Custom Type Flow** | User creates type → Submits to marketplace → Admin reviews → Approved/Rejected → Webhook fires |

### Task 4.2 — Cross-System Consistency
| ID | Task | Details |
|----|------|---------|
| 4.2.1 | Stripe ↔ DB plan sync | `customer.subscription.updated` correctly updates user plan |
| 4.2.2 | Admin panel ↔ SaaS data | Plans created in admin appear in SaaS pricing |
| 4.2.3 | Redis ↔ DB feature flags | Flag changes propagate within cache TTL (60s) |
| 4.2.4 | Webhook events ↔ deliveries | All 16 event types fire correct payloads |
| 4.2.5 | Usage tracking ↔ limits | API calls counted match `api_usage_events` records |

---

## PHASE 5: SECURITY HARDENING

### Task 5.1 — Critical Security
| ID | Task | Risk | Files |
|----|------|------|-------|
| 5.1.1 | **Fix SSRF gaps in webhook URL validation** | Missing `0.0.0.0`, `169.254.*`, IPv6 private ranges, DNS rebinding | `app/api/webhooks/route.ts` |
| 5.1.2 | **Fix XSS in sanitize utility** | Entity decoding re-introduces tags | `lib/sanitize.ts` |
| 5.1.3 | **Audit API key storage** | Verify raw keys never logged, only hash stored | `lib/api-key.ts`, `app/api/api-keys/route.ts` |
| 5.1.4 | **Verify CSP headers** | Current CSP has `unsafe-inline` for scripts — tighten with nonces | `next.config.ts` |
| 5.1.5 | **Stripe webhook signature verification** | Ensure `constructEvent` uses raw body, not parsed JSON | `app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts` |

### Task 5.2 — Auth & Access Control
| ID | Task | Details |
|----|------|---------|
| 5.2.1 | Verify admin session 8h expiry enforcement | `verifyAdmin` checks `hoursSinceLogin > 8` |
| 5.2.2 | Verify API key scope enforcement | `hasScope()` called before all scoped operations |
| 5.2.3 | Verify resource ownership checks | `verifyOwnership()` used on all user-specific mutations |
| 5.2.4 | Test admin privilege escalation | Non-admin user cannot access admin API routes |
| 5.2.5 | Test suspended user access | Suspended users blocked from all operations |

### Task 5.3 — Injection & Input Validation
| ID | Task | Details |
|----|------|---------|
| 5.3.1 | SQL injection testing | Drizzle ORM parameterizes queries — verify no raw SQL |
| 5.3.2 | XSS testing on all user inputs | QR names, webhook URLs, form fields |
| 5.3.3 | CSV injection in bulk upload | `sanitizeCSVCell` covers all dangerous chars |
| 5.3.4 | Webhook payload spoofing | `verifyWebhookSignature` uses `timingSafeEqual` |

---

## PHASE 6: PERFORMANCE & PRODUCTION READINESS

### Task 6.1 — Performance
| ID | Task | Details |
|----|------|---------|
| 6.1.1 | Verify DB indexes on hot paths | `scan_events`, `api_usage_events`, `webhook_deliveries` |
